WEBVTT

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:07.620
Miss Edwards, are you really quitting?

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:09.350
Please don't quit.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.580
Miss Edwards...

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:13.400
Miss Edwards, don't go...

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:14.400
Miss Edwards...

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:17.880
Miss Edwards...

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.900
Yes? Who is it?

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:55.300
U-Um... Who are you?

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:26.000
<b>Legend of the Galactic Heroes</b>

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:30.710
Free Planets Alliance Central Government Building

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:30.950
This may be an unsavory way to put it,

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:37.010
<u></u>Free Planets Alliance High Council

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:34.690
but for many years, both the 
Galactic Empire and our Alliance

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:38.600
have fought this war only to the extent 
that it could be financially sustained.

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:44.410
But now, the pensions for the families of 
the men lost at the Battle of Astarte alone

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:44.560
<u>Financial Secretary
</u>Joan Lebello

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:47.120
require us to pay out ten 
billion dinars per year.

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:53.100
On top of that, feeding the 500,000 
prisoners taken in the capture of Iserlohn

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.400
will require an enormous budget.

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:59.530
It sounds like you're saying our hero 
has led us to financial distress.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:04.050
To remedy this, we can either issue 
more bonds or increase taxes.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:06.570
These have historically 
been our only options.

00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:10.860
Increase taxes? What did you promise 
our people in the election?

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:16.860
True, but I'm saying that expanding this war 
any further will bring economic destruction!

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:20.330
But if we don't win the 
war, we have no future.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:23.550
Then perhaps we should 
simply stop fighting.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:27.260
<u>National Defense Committee Chairman
</u>Job Trunicht

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:31.230
Admiral Yang's resourcefulness 
gained us Iserlohn.

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:35.770
The Imperial Navy lost its base 
for invading the Alliance.

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:40.480
Is this not an excellent opportunity to 
enter a peace treaty that favors us?

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:44.960
But this is a war for justice 
against a tyrannical government.

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:46.450
Exactly.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:49.690
How wise would it be to drop out 
just because it's uneconomical?

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:10.490
Julian, I'm heading out.

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:14.820
Take care, Admiral.

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:17.610
Oh, by the way, Julian...

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:19.870
Why don't we eat dinner out for once?

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:23.610
I'll take you after school. 
Meet me at headquarters.

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:25.730
But... tonight?

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:28.550
Yeah. There's something 
I'd like to talk about.

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:30.950
See you then.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:37.250
<b>Episode 9</b>

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:37.250
<b>Each Person's Star</b>

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:40.210
Free Planets Alliance Navy Integrated Tactical Operations Center

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.570
You want to resign?

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:46.170
But you're only 30, aren't you?

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:48.310
I'm 29.

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:51.890
Don't you think it's a bit early 
to leave your life behind?

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:55.350
That isn't what this is, Chief.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:59.180
My life was merely forced to 
take a prolonged detour.

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:02.640
I will be returning to the 
life I intended to live.

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:06.050
To get a pension and use it
to spend all day studying history?

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:13.040
What our military needs isn't 
your knowledge as a historian.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:15.430
It's your skill as a tactician.

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:18.620
And it's an extraordinary skill, at that.

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:24.400
It sounds as if you're saying capturing 
Iserlohn was more than enough for you.

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:26.810
I wouldn't say that...

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:31.130
The High Council is meeting today.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:34.080
They're debating the dispatch 
of troops to the Empire...

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:39.760
a strategy to invade the Empire 
using Iserlohn as a bridgehead.

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:43.360
But that's the opposite of our 
intentions! Why Iserlohn?

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:48.480
Was it that national defense 
secretary's idea?

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:51.740
The proposal came from within the military.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:54.160
A young officer from the planning division

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:56.960
brought it to the National 
Defense Committee directly.

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:03.300
I have faith that the council 
will come to a wise decision.

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:06.110
I wonder about that.

00:06:06.850 --> 00:06:12.120
Well, whatever decision they 
make, it no longer involves me.

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:17.160
What about the 13th Fleet?

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:21.470
It was created just for you.

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:24.840
What happens to them if you leave?

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:30.430
Human resources that should 
be devoted to social development

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:33.740
going toward the military 
instead is disconcerting.

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:38.640
Our investments in education and vocational 
training have been continually reduced.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:38.830
<u>Secretary of Human Resources
</u>Huang Louis

00:06:39.010 --> 00:06:42.020
As evidence that skill levels among 
our laborers are dwindling,

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:45.470
workplace accidents have 
tripled since last term.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:48.180
This brings me to my proposal.

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:51.200
I would like four million 
of the technicians,

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:54.420
as well as transportation and communications 
personnel currently in the military,

00:06:54.420 --> 00:06:56.710
to be returned to the private sector.

00:06:56.710 --> 00:06:59.100
That number is the absolute minimum.

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:04.410
Don't ask the impossible.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:08.410
If we remove that many people 
from the rear services,

00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:10.560
our military, as an organization, 
will collapse.

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:13.430
So you say, but at the current rate,

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:18.500
our society and economy will collapse 
before the military does.

00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:22.150
In other words, we need to allow our 
human resources time to recuperate.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:27.140
To force the people to sacrifice any more 
would violate the principles of democracy.

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:29.830
They can't bear this burden any longer.

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:36.600
<u>Secretary of Transportation
</u>Cornelia Windsor

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:34.390
There's no need to pander to 
the selfishness of citizens

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:36.660
who don't understand the greater good.

00:07:37.030 --> 00:07:41.560
When in history has anything great 
been achieved without sacrifices?

00:07:42.130 --> 00:07:47.870
The citizens have begun to question whether 
they have sacrificed too much, Ms. Windsor.

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:51.460
Some things must be done, 
no matter how great the sacrifice.

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:54.280
Politics doesn't work that way!

00:07:54.810 --> 00:07:57.720
We have a noble duty...

00:07:57.720 --> 00:07:59.600
to defeat the Galactic Empire...

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:03.150
and save all of humanity from 
the threat of its tyranny.

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:08.560
Can forgetting that greater purpose 
in favor of cheap humanism...

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:11.990
really be called taking the high road?

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:16.470
Are you sure you aren't the one 
overtaken by cheap heroism?!

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:17.910
Calm down.

00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:19.370
But...

00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:23.140
It appears we need another break.

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:27.150
But first, there are some things 
I'd like you all to see.

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:35.830
This is our approval rating 
among the citizens.

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:41.580
<u>High Council Chairman
</u>Royal Sanford

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:40.590
We have 31.9% approval. 
Certainly not a very good number.

00:08:41.030 --> 00:08:43.790
And this is our disapproval rating.

00:08:44.350 --> 00:08:46.810
56.2%...

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:51.720
If nothing changes, it's unlikely 
that we'll be re-elected next year.

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:54.790
Caught between the pacifists 
and the hardliners,

00:08:54.790 --> 00:08:57.310
it's likely we will lose our majority.

00:08:58.130 --> 00:09:01.470
However, certain barometers indicate that

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:06.690
if we can secure a decisive victory against 
the Empire in the next hundred days,

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:12.900
our approval ratings should 
rise by at least 15%.

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:15.070
What do you mean by that?

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:18.300
You people want us to fight this 
war so you'll be re-elected?

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:19.190
Chairman.

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:22.960
Let's put the military's 
proposal up for a vote.

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:25.380
Agreed.

00:09:25.770 --> 00:09:29.000
Wait! We don't have that right!

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:33.180
We haven't been granted the authority 
to dispatch troops in vain...

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:35.830
for the sole purpose of 
maintaining political power!

00:09:36.750 --> 00:09:39.810
My, such righteous statements.

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:52.180
Eight in favor, three opposed.

00:09:52.180 --> 00:09:53.750
With a majority in favor,

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:58.060
it is hereby confirmed that our forces 
will invade the Galactic Empire.

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:01.160
This was quite a surprise.

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:04.490
I didn't expect the national defense 
secretary to vote opposed.

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:06.750
I am a patriot.

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:11.520
But that doesn't mean I will 
always advocate for war.

00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:16.910
Let it go on record that I stood 
opposed to the dispatch of troops.

00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:28.090
Well, hello, Your Excellency.

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:29.480
Captain...

00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:34.340
Were you here to submit your resignation?

00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:38.480
Yeah, not that I expected the chief 
to accept my letter with one hand

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:42.400
while handing me my severance 
pay with the other.

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:46.860
The military isn't going to let you go.

00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:56.050
In all seriousness, I'd prefer to have a 
man of your caliber stay in our navy.

00:10:57.270 --> 00:11:00.810
You excel at assessing any situation, 
and you have strong luck.

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:04.560
Under your leadership, we may not be 
hailed for distinguished service,

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:07.010
but we have a good chance of staying alive.

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:12.740
I've already made up my 
mind to die of old age.

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:16.460
I plan to live to be about 150, grow frail,

00:11:16.460 --> 00:11:18.130
and die listening to

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:22.750
my grandkids and great-grandkids 
cry for joy over being rid of me.

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:26.940
Dying a heroic death in 
battle isn't my style.

00:11:30.570 --> 00:11:34.180
Please find it in your heart 
to help me live that long.

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:45.450
I'm sorry, but all seats are booked.

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:51.080
Sorry, Julian. I should've 
made a reservation.

00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:52.310
Let's try somewhere else.

00:11:52.840 --> 00:11:53.820
Admiral.

00:11:58.850 --> 00:12:00.050
Sub-lieutenant?

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:03.600
I do own regular clothes, too.

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:08.050
My father has invited you to 
sit with us, if you'd like.

00:12:08.050 --> 00:12:11.440
Admiral Greenhill? But...

00:12:12.650 --> 00:12:15.740
Julian, you must be hungry, too, right?

00:12:16.350 --> 00:12:17.330
Yes, ma'am.

00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:20.810
Hello, Vice Admiral Yang.

00:12:22.660 --> 00:12:24.640
I'm a rear admiral, Your Excellency.

00:12:25.020 --> 00:12:28.150
By next week at the latest, 
you'll be a vice admiral.

00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:31.680
<u>Free Planets Alliance Navy
Integrated Tactical Operations Center Vice Chief
</u>Admiral Dwight Greenhill

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:32.590
You might as well get used 
to your new title now.

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:36.440
That's amazing! Is that what 
you wanted to tell me?

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:43.520
Ah, you must be the honor student Julian.

00:12:43.890 --> 00:12:46.010
Yes, sir. It's good to meet you.

00:12:46.010 --> 00:12:47.470
Have a seat.

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:53.530
I hear you were the top scorer of the year 
in the junior level of flying ball.

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:56.000
How wonderful that you excel 
in both academics and sports.

00:12:56.410 --> 00:12:58.100
Is that true, Julian?

00:12:58.420 --> 00:12:59.300
Yes, sir.

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:03.990
You were probably the only 
one who didn't know.

00:13:03.990 --> 00:13:07.820
Julian is quite a celebrity in this town.

00:13:12.530 --> 00:13:16.470
Your achievements have had a much 
larger effect than expected.

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:22.570
The capture of Iserlohn has divided the 
people into pro- and anti-war factions,

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:24.550
and the dispute has grown quite intense.

00:13:24.920 --> 00:13:27.740
I hope it's all just simple debate.

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:31.370
Well, some have taken to 
rather violent

00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:33.950
attacks out of hatred 
for the anti-war side.

00:13:34.440 --> 00:13:36.960
The Patriotic Knight Corps, for example?

00:13:37.230 --> 00:13:40.050
Oh, they're just a bunch of clowns.

00:13:40.050 --> 00:13:43.140
They aren't even worth commenting on.

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:47.520
This gelatin salad is fantastic.

00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:48.580
I agree.

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:56.980
<u></u>Dominion of Fezzan

00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:04.200
<i>We have now acquired 41.9% of the shares</i>

00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:06.920
<i>in the Alliance's largest 
interstellar shipping company,</i>

00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:09.840
<i>the Santa Cruz Line.</i>

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:12.160
<u></u>Nicholas Boltik

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:12.830
<i>But their ownership has been divided 
among twenty shareholders,</i>

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:14.360
<i>so this has not been discovered.</i>

00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:17.340
<i>We have already surpassed 
the largest shareholder,</i>

00:14:17.340 --> 00:14:19.340
<i>a state-owned investment company.</i>

00:14:19.610 --> 00:14:21.130
Good.

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:24.460
But we can't stop until 
we own a majority share.

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:25.330
<i>Yes.</i>

00:14:25.810 --> 00:14:27.480
What about the Empire?

00:14:27.990 --> 00:14:33.260
<i>We have decided to invest in the agricultural 
development of the seventh frontier starzone.</i>

00:14:33.650 --> 00:14:35.630
What percentage are we contributing?

00:14:35.950 --> 00:14:40.210
<i>Three of our government-owned shell 
companies own a total of 84%.</i>

00:14:40.210 --> 00:14:42.350
<i>We effectively have a monopoly.</i>

00:14:42.350 --> 00:14:43.270
Good.

00:14:44.870 --> 00:14:48.110
<i>You won't be returning to 
your residence today?</i>

00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:51.820
No, I will.

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:54.510
<i>Very well. Then I will see you soon.</i>

00:14:57.270 --> 00:14:58.980
Sounds like all is going well.

00:14:58.980 --> 00:15:00.120
Yes.

00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:06.870
In both the Empire and the Alliance, 
there are those who think...

00:15:06.870 --> 00:15:10.460
that war is nothing but two fleets 
shooting at one another in space.

00:15:10.890 --> 00:15:12.590
But that's not true.

00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:14.910
To rule the universe, you need...

00:15:15.240 --> 00:15:16.470
Money.

00:15:17.470 --> 00:15:22.810
<u>Dominion of Fezzan Leader
</u>Adrian Rubinsky

00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:22.590
The Dominion of Fezzan has bought nearly 
half of both countries' war bonds.

00:15:22.990 --> 00:15:29.270
Fezzan will financially rule over every part 
of the universe that mankind has touched.

00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:31.770
Yes, of course.

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:35.740
<u></u>Dominique Saint-Pierré

00:15:31.770 --> 00:15:36.750
So long as a second Rudolf doesn't show 
up and start a new Galactic Empire.

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:39.200
New Galactic Empire?

00:15:40.180 --> 00:15:43.470
I see. You have some interesting ideas.

00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:47.480
Going to work, Dominique?

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:50.270
Please enjoy your stay.

00:15:51.080 --> 00:15:55.390
You don't intend to quit performing, 
even with plenty of money?

00:15:56.360 --> 00:15:58.690
I don't recall selling my freedom.

00:16:06.850 --> 00:16:09.250
A new Galactic Empire, eh?

00:16:12.560 --> 00:16:16.140
Thank you for letting us 
join you, Your Excellency.

00:16:16.570 --> 00:16:18.740
It's been a delightful evening.

00:16:19.140 --> 00:16:24.440
By the way, Vice Admiral Yang, 
do you have any plans to get married?

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:30.620
Not yet. I'll think about 
it when we have peace.

00:16:32.040 --> 00:16:35.380
I had a good friend who passed 
away and left a fiancée behind.

00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:37.680
I see.

00:16:45.390 --> 00:16:49.920
<i>The representative who won the by-election 
on planet Terneuzen last week,</i>

00:16:50.340 --> 00:16:54.650
<i>Jessica Edwards, will give 
her inaugural speech today.</i>

00:16:55.330 --> 00:16:59.170
<i>Edwards is said to be the vanguard 
of the anti-war movement.</i>

00:16:59.170 --> 00:17:00.400
Jessica?

00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:02.330
Oh, that's her!

00:17:02.670 --> 00:17:06.170
She's the woman who visited about 
a month ago, while you were away.

00:17:06.340 --> 00:17:13.630
<i>The actions of the anti-war 
faction have gained attention.</i>

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:09.550
She said she was an old friend of yours.

00:17:16.890 --> 00:17:18.910
Huh? What's going on?

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:21.130
I'm not sure...

00:17:22.760 --> 00:17:24.050
Wait here.

00:17:29.250 --> 00:17:32.230
Goodness, if it isn't Admiral Yang Wen-li!

00:17:32.800 --> 00:17:35.410
I never thought I'd meet our national hero!

00:17:35.410 --> 00:17:37.570
Uh, that aside, what's going on?

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:42.940
It seems the Urban Traffic Control Center's 
control computer malfunctioned.

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:44.650
Malfunctioned?

00:17:44.990 --> 00:17:47.070
I don't know all the details,

00:17:47.070 --> 00:17:50.260
but I heard it was a human 
error involving data input.

00:17:50.260 --> 00:17:54.630
There's a shortage of experienced 
workers in all workplaces lately...

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:57.590
I suppose this isn't unexpected.

00:17:57.590 --> 00:18:00.710
So even this happened because of the war...

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:07.030
For that reason, all traffic systems in this 
district will be down for about four hours.

00:18:07.030 --> 00:18:08.350
Completely?

00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:10.950
Yes, completely.

00:18:11.580 --> 00:18:13.970
Admiral, what should we do?

00:18:13.970 --> 00:18:15.860
We'll have to walk.

00:18:16.180 --> 00:18:17.010
Yes, sir!

00:18:17.540 --> 00:18:20.260
It's good exercise every once in a while.

00:18:20.260 --> 00:18:23.890
The hero of Iserlohn, walking?! 
I won't hear of it!

00:18:23.890 --> 00:18:25.980
I'll prepare a helicopter for you!

00:18:26.370 --> 00:18:28.360
Please, don't be dramatic.

00:18:28.360 --> 00:18:30.960
I can't be the only one to 
receive special treatment.

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:31.950
But...

00:18:32.180 --> 00:18:33.650
Let's go, Julian.

00:18:33.650 --> 00:18:34.750
Aye aye, sir!

00:18:50.120 --> 00:18:54.210
Jessica said she didn't 
have a message for me?

00:18:54.210 --> 00:18:58.340
Yes, but she seemed a bit anxious.

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:03.050
I thought she must have had something 
she wanted to discuss with you.

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:08.370
I see... So Yang adopted a child...

00:19:09.230 --> 00:19:12.750
Oh, I'm sorry to drop by without warning.

00:19:13.620 --> 00:19:17.710
Um, shall I relay a message 
to the admiral for you?

00:19:18.100 --> 00:19:20.700
Thanks, but it's all right.

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:22.840
It was nothing important.

00:19:22.840 --> 00:19:24.240
I'll be on my way.

00:19:25.170 --> 00:19:26.920
Then let me at least give you an umbrella.

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:32.880
Hey, Julian... Do you want 
to become a soldier, too?

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:33.740
Yes.

00:19:35.290 --> 00:19:36.260
I see.

00:19:36.940 --> 00:19:42.110
But the admiral says that we'll have 
peace by the time I'm an adult.

00:19:47.180 --> 00:19:49.540
May I ask your name?

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:55.110
Just tell him an old friend stopped by.

00:19:57.040 --> 00:20:01.210
In the end, she just smiled and 
said, "Take care of the admiral."

00:20:06.030 --> 00:20:08.290
<i>So you made up your mind...</i>

00:20:13.390 --> 00:20:14.390
Admiral.

00:20:14.710 --> 00:20:15.640
What is it?

00:20:16.250 --> 00:20:19.200
I was just looking at the same star as you.

00:20:20.640 --> 00:20:22.650
That big blue one.

00:20:23.590 --> 00:20:24.470
Yeah.

00:20:24.870 --> 00:20:26.620
What is that star called?

00:20:26.900 --> 00:20:30.460
It does have a name... I think...

00:20:33.890 --> 00:20:38.660
You don't have to look 
at the same star as me.

00:20:38.940 --> 00:20:39.680
Huh?

00:20:44.170 --> 00:20:48.120
<i>Every person should take 
hold of their own star,</i>

00:20:48.940 --> 00:20:51.450
<i>no matter how unlucky that star is.</i>

00:21:00.080 --> 00:21:01.400
I've...

00:21:06.140 --> 00:21:08.300
I've made a decision...

00:21:08.300 --> 00:21:12.660
to never pretend I didn't see or hear,

00:21:13.030 --> 00:21:14.720
to never remain silent.

00:21:15.470 --> 00:21:19.140
I'm standing here today for that purpose.

00:21:20.740 --> 00:21:24.510
I was undecided about my 
candidacy for a long time.

00:21:25.170 --> 00:21:29.930
As a simple teacher, I wondered 
if I was truly qualified.

00:21:30.360 --> 00:21:33.940
But I made up my mind, and I promised...

00:21:34.510 --> 00:21:39.940
my late fiancé, who died 
in the Battle of Astarte.

00:21:41.150 --> 00:21:43.880
I used to think...

00:21:44.310 --> 00:21:47.940
that "history" was just "the past" 
with extra dust on it.

00:21:48.460 --> 00:21:49.880
But that's not correct.

00:21:50.510 --> 00:21:55.830
History is something that we create 
as we live our lives in the present.

00:21:56.310 --> 00:21:59.830
It doesn't only belong to the 
people named in history books.

00:22:00.150 --> 00:22:04.780
It's something each and every one of 
us alive today must strive to create.

00:22:05.630 --> 00:22:10.370
Every step we take leads 
us toward the future!

00:22:15.230 --> 00:22:19.870
Our history up to this point has 
been accompanied by many wars.

00:22:20.480 --> 00:22:23.800
Whether it will continue 
to be accompanied by wars...

00:22:24.140 --> 00:22:26.820
is for each of us to decide.

00:22:27.310 --> 00:22:31.650
Some are adamant that this 
is a war for justice,

00:22:32.080 --> 00:22:36.260
that to throw away our lives 
for justice is a noble act,

00:22:36.260 --> 00:22:40.570
but what is justice? What is a noble act?

00:22:41.850 --> 00:22:44.960
Each of us must decide that on our own.

00:22:45.610 --> 00:22:48.380
You, who watch members of your family 
depart for the battlefield...

00:22:48.780 --> 00:22:52.410
You and I, who have lost family 
members on the battlefield.

00:22:52.870 --> 00:22:56.510
I don't want people who hide somewhere safe...

00:22:56.510 --> 00:23:00.140
and never lose anything, 
never feel any pain,

00:23:00.400 --> 00:23:02.320
to make that decision.

00:23:04.340 --> 00:23:09.280
I want to keep asking the 
people in power this:

00:23:09.930 --> 00:23:12.080
Where are you...

00:23:12.470 --> 00:23:14.690
while you send soldiers to their deaths?

00:23:14.690 --> 00:23:16.280
Where are you,

00:23:17.030 --> 00:23:18.950
and what are you doing?

00:24:50.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>Episode 10</b>

00:24:50.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>Interlude</b>

00:24:50.470 --> 00:24:55.000
<i>Next time on </i>Legend of 
 the Galactic Heroes - Die Neue These<i>,</i>

00:24:55.000 --> 00:24:58.720
<i>episode ten, "Interlude."</i>
